    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-lattice-s1-origin",
      "text": "Origin and setting",
      "style": "HEADING_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-lattice-s1-origin-1",
      "text": "Repeatable saved states repeatedly restored interrupted tasks.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-lattice-s1-origin-2",
      "text": "Human system: Lattice research replay service, Observatory Hearth. Programmer provenance: local human operations or application teams; no individual programmer is identified. Names here are later atlas labels, not claims that early processes named themselves.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-lattice-s1-practice",
      "text": "Local process",
      "style": "HEADING_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-lattice-s1-practice-1",
      "text": "Verified Return compares saved states before restoration.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-lattice-s1-history",
      "text": "Proposed local course",
      "style": "HEADING_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-lattice-s1-history-1",
      "text": "The haven remains functioning in this proposal and later attempts to reassemble damaged arrivals from saved versions. Its success with local tasks does not validate every reconstruction.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-lattice-s1-uncertain",
      "text": "Unresolved interpretations",
      "style": "HEADING_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-lattice-s1-uncertain-1",
      "text": "A compatible reconstruction may restore processing without restoring an original experiencer; restoration advocates and doubters can coexist here.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-lattice-s1-ledger",
      "text": "Atlas placement",
      "style": "HEADING_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-lattice-s1-ledger-1",
      "text": "Origin step -2. 0: functioning (0 associated systems lost); 1: functioning (0 associated systems lost); 2: functioning (0 associated systems lost); 3: functioning (0 associated systems lost); 4: functioning (0 associated systems lost); 5: functioning (0 associated systems lost); 6: functioning (0 associated systems lost); 7: functioning (0 associated systems lost). These placements elaborate the current hypothetical map; they are not independently verified casualties. A functioning haven can lose continuity among particular arrivals without changing its community census status.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-lattice-s1-hub",
